<section><div class="wrap feature-lead"><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">Battery runway</span><h2>Put a date beside the decline.</h2><p>Once there is enough history, WhatBattery fits a trend through the Mac's recorded health and estimates when it may reach 80%, the point Apple uses as a service reference.</p><p>It also reports the recent wear rate and flags when the battery begins ageing faster than its own established pattern.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>No forecast until there is enough evidence</li><li>Projected 80% date and time remaining</li><li>Recent wear rate in plain language</li><li>Faster-than-trend warning</li></ul></div><img src="/img/screenshot-history.png" alt="Long-term battery health history in WhatBattery" width="440" /></div></section>

<section class="soft-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-tag">Two kinds of history</span><h2>Inspect the session. Keep the lifetime record.</h2><p>Dense telemetry helps explain what happened during a charge or drain. Sparse monthly health records show the slower wear story across every device.</p></div><div class="card-grid two"><article class="card"><h3>Lifetime Analyzer</h3><p>Explore charge, temperature, voltage, and power over a selected range, with minimum, average, and maximum values.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Health History</h3><p>Keep one durable record per device per day, rolled into monthly health and cycle summaries for Macs, iPhones, and iPads.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section id="reports"><div class="wrap feature-lead"><img src="/img/screenshot-report.png" alt="A one-page WhatBattery battery report ready to save as PDF or print" width="620" loading="lazy" /><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">Reports and export</span><h2>Keep the evidence when the battery matters.</h2><p>Turn the current reading and lifetime summary into a one-page PDF or printout for a warranty claim, a Genius Bar visit, or a resale listing.</p><p>For deeper analysis, export recorded samples as CSV or JSON. Health history can also be backed up and restored.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>One-page PDF and print report</li><li>CSV and JSON sample export</li><li>Long-term health backup and restore</li></ul></div></div></section>

